# Next.js 15 & React 19 Standards
Adapted from `pontusab/cursorrules` and `midudev/cursor-rules`.

## Server vs. Client Components
- **Default to React Server Components (RSC)**: All files in `src/app/**/page.tsx` and helper components are Server Components by default.
- **`'use client'` Boundary**: Only place `'use client'` at the top of components that strictly require:
  - Interactive event handlers (`onClick`, `onChange`, `onSubmit`).
  - React State or Effects (`useState`, `useReducer`, `useEffect`, `useRef`).
  - Browser APIs (`window`, `localStorage`, `navigator.geolocation`, camera/MediaDevices).
- **Component Decomposition**:
  - Keep client components at leaf nodes of the component tree.
  - Fetch data on the server and pass data as props to client leaves, or compose client wrappers around server children (`children` prop).

## Next.js 15 Route Conventions
- **Asynchronous `params` and `searchParams`**:
  In Next.js 15, route params and searchParams are Promises:
  ```tsx
  interface PageProps {
    params: Promise<{ id: string }>;
    searchParams: Promise<{ [key: string]: string | string[] | undefined }>;
  }

  export default async function Page({ params, searchParams }: PageProps) {
    const { id } = await params;
    const resolvedSearchParams = await searchParams;
    // ...
  }
  ```

## UI & Styling with Tailwind CSS v4
- Use semantic utility classes from Tailwind CSS v4.
- Follow mobile-first design: structure elements for mobile screens first, then enhance with `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:`, `xl:`.
- **User Feedback & Loading States**:
  - Disable buttons (`disabled={isLoading}`) during async actions and show a spinning `Loader2` from `lucide-react`.
  - Use toast notifications (`react-hot-toast` or similar) for immediate feedback on submit/save/delete.
  - Standard status colors:
    - Success/Hadir: `text-emerald-600 bg-emerald-50 dark:bg-emerald-950/30 dark:text-emerald-400`
    - Warning/Terlambat: `text-amber-600 bg-amber-50 dark:bg-amber-950/30 dark:text-amber-400`
    - Error/Ditolak: `text-rose-600 bg-rose-50 dark:bg-rose-950/30 dark:text-rose-400`
    - Neutral/Info: `text-slate-700 bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300`

## Performance & Optimization
- Use `next/image` (`Image`) with proper `width`, `height`, or `fill` with `sizes` for any static or uploaded images.
- Avoid passing massive unneeded payload objects over the RSC-to-Client component boundary.
- For icons, import individually from `lucide-react` (tree-shaken).

